// Kioto 3.0.0 — math module (placeholder).
//
// The 3.0 math surface is a from-scratch pure-Mire rewrite: every function is
// computed in Mire itself, with no rt_math_* runtime dependency and no math.c
// linked into the final binary. That is why this file starts empty instead of
// carrying the 2.x code over.
//
// The 2.x layout (angle, constants, float_manip, number_theoretic) does not map
// onto the 3.0 layout, so nothing here is a mechanical port.
//
// Submodules land one at a time, in this order:
//   consts, seq, int, float, sum, stats, complex, decimal, random,
//   power, trig, hyperbolic, special
//
// See todo.md for the per-symbol inventory and the accuracy rules.
